WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Oil sands operations contribute significant carbon emissions in Canada. So the six largest companies have teamed up to make strides on the path to NetZero. Investing in technology and innovation. Already cut emissions an average 22% per barrel. Working with governments to create and protect jobs. Developing one of the world's largest carbon capture and storage facilities. Our NetZero plan is in motion and we're making progress on multiple pathways. See our plan in action at pathwaysalliance.ca
加拿大油砂开采产生了大量的碳排放。因此，六家最大的公司携手合作，在迈向净零排放的道路上大步迈进。他们投资于技术和创新，已将每桶石油的平均排放量降低了 22%。他们与政府合作创造和保护就业岗位，并开发了世界上最大的碳捕集与储存设施之一。我们的净零计划正在实施中，我们正通过多种途径取得进展。请访问 pathwaysalliance.ca 查看我们的行动计划。

2
00:00:30.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Music Our episodes deal with serious and often distressing incidents. If you feel at any time you need support, please contact your local crisis centre. For suggested phone numbers for confidential support, please see the show notes for this episode on your app or on our website. 21 year old University of Texas student Mark Kilroy was excited about spring break. 1989 had been a busy year for the pre-med student and he was looking forward to some downtime before taking his upcoming medical college admission test. Mark had made plans with three old high school friends to head to South Padre Island on the southern coastal tip of Texas. A trip he had made for spring break twice before.
音乐 我们的节目涉及严重且往往令人痛心的事件。如果您在任何时候觉得需要支持，请联系您当地的危机中心。有关保密支持的建议电话号码，请查看您手机应用上或我们网站上的本集节目说明。21 岁的德克萨斯大学学生马克·基尔罗伊对春假充满期待。1989 年对于这位预科医学生来说是忙碌的一年，他一直期待在参加即将到来的医学院入学考试前能有一些放松的时间。马克与三位老高中朋友计划前往德克萨斯州南端南帕德雷岛。他以前曾为春假去过那里两次。

3
00:01:31.000 --> 00:02:49.000
Bordered by the Gulf of Mexico to the east and to the long shallow Laguna Madre to the west, South Padre Island boasts a warm subtropical climate typical of the area. After sustaining severe damage from Hurricane Bula in 1967, the island's town was rebuilt with resorts and condos cropping up along the coastline. A tourism boom in the late 1980s established South Padre Island as a popular vacation destination, especially for young spring breakers. In March 1989 alone, the island's population rose from 1,000 to 250,000 as students from all over the United States arrived for a week of beachside partying. Mark Kilroy and his friend Bradley Moore had been discussing spring break since the beginning of the fall semester. The pair attended different Texas-based universities but maintained their friendship by phoning each other at least twice a week. On Friday, March 10, Bradley picked Mark up from his campus in Austin to begin their journey to South Padre Island. They then collected Bill Huddleston and Brett Martin.
南帕德雷岛东临墨西哥湾，西接漫长而浅的拉古纳马德雷，拥有该地区典型的温暖亚热带气候。在 1967 年遭受飓风布拉的严重破坏后，该岛的小镇进行了重建，海岸线上涌现出度假村和公寓。20 世纪 80 年代末的旅游业繁荣确立了南帕德雷岛作为热门度假胜地的地位，尤其是对年轻的春假狂欢者而言。仅在 1989 年 3 月，随着来自全美各地的学生涌入进行为期一周的海滩派对，该岛的人口就从 1,000 人激增至 250,000 人。马克·基尔罗伊和他的朋友布拉德利·穆尔从秋季学期开始就一直在讨论春假。两人就读于德克萨斯州不同的大学，但每周至少通电话两次以维持友谊。3 月 10 日星期五，布拉德利从奥斯汀的校园接上马克，开始了前往南帕德雷岛的旅程。然后他们去接了比尔·赫德尔斯顿和布雷特·马丁。

4
00:02:49.000 --> 00:04:01.000
All four were longtime friends having played basketball and baseball together in high school before disbanding after graduation. They hadn't seen much of each other since and the trip afforded them a long-awaited catch-up. During the four-hour drive to the island, they discussed their upcoming plans for the summer and reflected on how it would likely be their last time in Texas together. The group checked into the Sheraton Hotels and Resorts around mid-morning on Saturday, March 11. Spring break had only just begun and the hotel was still quiet but staff had removed the furniture in the lobby in preparation for the influx of students. Their first two days were spent at the beach behind their hotel, taking advantage of the free entertainment on offer including concerts, movies and parties. Four days into the break on Tuesday, March 14, Lieutenant George Gavito was on duty at the Brownsville Sheriff's Office in Southern Texas when three young men arrived wanting to speak to somebody about one of their friends.
这四人是多年的老朋友，曾在高中一起打篮球和棒球，毕业后各奔东西。自那以后他们见面的机会不多，这次旅行让他们得到了期待已久的聚叙。在驱车前往该岛的四个小时里，他们讨论了即将到来的夏天计划，并反思这可能是他们最后一次一起在德克萨斯州了。3 月 11 日星期六上午，这群人入住喜来登酒店及度假村。春假才刚刚开始，酒店依然很安静，但工作人员已经移走了大厅里的家具，为涌入的学生做准备。他们头两天是在酒店后面的海滩上度过的，享受着提供的免费娱乐活动，包括音乐会、电影和派对。3 月 14 日星期二，即假期开始的第四天，乔治·加维托中尉正在德克萨斯州南部的布朗斯维尔警长办公室值班，当时有三个年轻人前来，想找人谈谈他们其中一个朋友的事。

5
00:04:01.000 --> 00:05:55.000
Bradley Moore, Bill Huddleston and Brett Martin informed the Lieutenant that Mark Kilroy was missing. On the second night of their vacation, Mark's group ventured to the city of Matamoros in northeastern Mexico. Located in the state of Tama-Lepus on the bank of the Rio Grande River, Matamoros is directly across the border from the city of Brownsville on the southernmost tip of Texas. With a population of over a million people, Matamoros was a hotspot for drug trafficking but was considered a safe destination for travelers. The area offered cheap alcohol and lax drinking laws, drawing America's youth to the festive local bars, nightclubs and restaurants. Moving between Brownsville and Matamoros required crossing over the Rio Grande via the Gateway International Bridge, an official port of entry along the two countries' borders. On Sunday, March 12, 1989, Mark Kilroy and his crew drove to Brownsville where they left their car before walking across the Gateway International Bridge into Mexico. They spent the night socializing at Sergeant Pepper's nightclub until around 2.30am when they returned to Texas and made their way back to South Padre Island.
布拉德利·穆尔、比尔·赫德尔斯顿和布雷特·马丁向中尉报告说马克·基尔罗伊失踪了。在假期的第二晚，马克的小组冒险去了墨西哥东北部的马塔莫罗斯市。马塔莫罗斯位于格兰德河畔的塔毛利帕斯州，位于德克萨斯州最南端布朗斯维尔市的正对岸。马塔莫罗斯人口超过一百万，是毒品走私的热点地区，但被认为是对旅行者安全的目的地。该地区提供廉价的酒精和宽松的饮酒法律，吸引了美国的年轻人前往节日般的当地酒吧、夜总会和餐厅。在布朗斯维尔和马塔莫罗斯之间穿梭需要经由网关国际大桥跨越格兰德河，这是两国边境沿线的一个官方入境口岸。1989 年 3 月 12 日星期日，马克·基尔罗伊和他的同伴开车到布朗斯维尔，把车留下，然后步行穿过网关国际大桥进入墨西哥。他们在佩珀中士夜总会社交到凌晨 2 点 30 分左右，随后返回德克萨斯州并返回南帕德雷岛。

6
00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:53.000
The group decided to venture back to Matamoros the following night of Monday, March 13. The city was a hive of activity, with approximately 15,000 spring breakers traversing the crowded main streets. The four friends wandered down the first thoroughfare after the bridge, the nightclub-lined Avenida Álvaro Obregon. Bill Huddleston described the area. It was like an amusement park but without the rides. It was one big thrill, the energy that was created by thousands and thousands of students. They entered the bar with the shortest line out front, Los Sombreros, then headed to the Hard Rock Cafe where Mark met some girls and separated from his friends. The crowds were dispersing by 2am and Bill suggested to Bradley and Brent that they go back to their hotel.
该小组决定在第二天晚上，即 3 月 13 日星期星期一再次冒险前往马塔莫罗斯。这座城市活动频繁，大约有 15,000 名春假狂欢者穿梭在拥挤的主干道上。四个朋友沿着桥后的第一条大道闲逛，那是林立着夜总会的阿尔瓦罗·奥布雷贡大道。比尔·赫德尔斯顿这样描述该地区：“这就像一个游乐园，只是没有游乐设施。成千上万的学生所产生的能量带来了一场巨大的狂欢。”他们走进了排队最短的酒吧“太阳帽”，然后前往硬石餐厅，在那里马克遇到了一些女孩并与朋友们分开了。到了凌晨 2 点，人群开始散去，比尔建议布拉德利和布雷特回酒店。

7
00:06:53.000 --> 00:08:04.000
The trio exited the bar and spotted Mark talking to a girl he had befriended on South Padre Island days earlier. He rejoined the group as they slowly made their way down the few blocks towards the Gateway International Bridge. The four tried to stay close to one another in a shoulder-to-shoulder formation but inevitably split into pairs as they navigated the thousands of intoxicated students moving aimlessly around the street. Bradley and Brent were ahead with Bill and Mark a few yards behind. When they reached the front of Garcia's, a one-story red and grey brick building that served as a local watering hole and gift shop, Mark stopped to say goodbye to the girl he'd been speaking to as Bill ran off to find somewhere secluded to urinate. When Bill re-emerged, Mark was nowhere to be seen. Assuming he must have continued onwards, Bill reached the bridge where Bradley and Brent were waiting. They called out for Mark but he didn't appear.
三人走出酒吧，发现马克正在和一个几天前在南帕德雷岛结识的女孩聊天。他重新加入了队伍，大家慢慢地沿着几条街向网关国际大桥走去。四人试图并肩保持紧密靠拢，但在数千名在街上漫无目的地移动的醉酒学生中穿行时，不可避免地分成了两组。布拉德利和布雷特在前，比尔和马克在几码后。当他们到达加西亚餐厅（一座用作当地饮水处和礼品店的单层红灰色砖砌建筑）门前时，马克停下来向他一直在交谈的女孩道别，而比尔则跑开去找隐蔽的地方小便。当比尔再次出现时，马克已经不见踪影。比尔以为他一定继续前行了，便来到了布拉德利和布雷特等待的桥边。他们大声呼唤马克，但他没有出现。

8
00:08:04.000 --> 00:09:26.000
They were immediately concerned. Mark wasn't the type to abandon the group or go elsewhere without telling them. Thinking Mark may have already crossed the bridge, his friends returned to Brownsville but he wasn't waiting by their car as anticipated. After waiting several minutes, they headed back into Matamoros to search for him. They scoured the nightclubs and bars until 4.30am by which point the streets were mostly empty but they couldn't find Mark anywhere. The trio drove back to South Padre Island hoping he had returned to their hotel on his own but there was no sign of him there either. The group considered the possibility that Mark had been thrown in jail and returned to Matamoros the following day to check the local police stations but to now avail. Officers expressed little concern as visiting students were often reported missing while partying in town but typically reappeared unharmed a few days later with nothing more than a hangover. Certain this wasn't the case with Mark, his friends went back to Brownsville to speak with police there.
他们立刻感到担忧。马克不是那种会抛弃团队或在不打招呼的情况下独自离开的人。朋友们以为马克可能已经过桥了，便返回布朗斯维尔，但他并没有像预期那样在车旁等待。等待了几分钟后，他们又返回马塔莫罗斯寻找他。他们搜寻了夜总会和酒吧直到凌晨 4 点半，此时街道大多空无一人，但他们到处都找不到马克。三人开车回到南帕德雷岛，希望他已经独自回到了酒店，但在那里也没有他的踪迹。这群人考虑了马克被关进监狱的可能性，并在第二天返回马塔莫罗斯检查当地的警察局，但无济于事。警官们对此并不太在意，因为来访的学生在镇上狂欢时经常被报失踪，但通常几天宿醉过后就会无恙地重新出现。确信马克并非如此，他的朋友们回到布朗斯维尔与那里的警察交谈。

9
00:09:26.000 --> 00:10:53.000
Lieutenant George Gavito suggested that Mark may have left with the girl he had spent the night talking to but his friends insisted he was not that type of person and would never leave without telling them his plans. Lieutenant Gavito filed a missing persons report and Bill, Brent and Bradley visited the US consulate while intermittently returning to their hotel to check if Mark had returned. When Mark hadn't shown up by 11pm on Tuesday night they contacted his parents, James and Helen. The Kilroy family were close knit with Mark the eldest of two sons. Bill Huddleston recalled feeling a tremendous sense of loss breaking the news as the reality of the situation sunk in. Mark's unexplained disappearance was of great concern to his parents as their clean cut firstborn was not a big partier nor was he a loo for careless but a leader who always gave 110%. He excelled both academically and athletically as a former boy scout, honours student and student council member who was skilled at basketball, baseball and golf. Following high school, Mark earned a basketball scholarship that he put aside to focus on his goal to become a general practice doctor.
乔治·加维托中尉暗示马克可能是和那个共度一晚的女孩一起离开的，但他的朋友们坚称他不是那种人，绝不会在没有告知计划的情况下离开。加维托中尉提交了一份失踪人口报告，比尔、布雷特和布拉德利访问了美国领事馆，同时断断续续地返回酒店检查马克是否已经回来。到了周二晚上 11 点马克仍未露面，他们联系了他的父母詹姆斯和海伦。基尔罗伊一家关系紧密，马克是两个儿子中的老大。比尔·赫德尔斯顿回忆说，当现实情况袭来时，宣布这一消息让他感到巨大的失落感。马克莫名其妙的失踪让他的父母非常担忧，因为他们品学兼优的长子并不是一个爱狂欢的人，也不是一个粗心大意的人，而是一个总是付出 110% 努力的领袖。他曾在学业和体育上表现出色，曾是童子军、荣誉学生和学生会成员，擅长篮球、棒球和高尔夫。高中毕业后，马克获得了一项篮球奖学金，但他将其搁置一边，专注于成为一名全科医生的目标。

10
00:10:53.000 --> 00:12:11.000
His former high school basketball coach Terry Ray stated, You always knew whatever he was doing out there, if it was Mark, it would be okay. Mark's uncle worked at the US Custom Service in Los Angeles and to use his connections to draw more attention to his nephew's disappearance. A task force to front the search was established in Brownsville despite American police having no jurisdiction to investigate in Mexico. Mexican police attempted to shift blame by alleging Mark had disappeared in Texas even though his friends firmly denied these claims. Realising the incident made discourage spring breakers from returning to Matamoros, government officials pressured local police to act. Within 48 hours of Mark's disappearance, the Mexican federal and state judicial police joined the US task force as investigators on both sides of the border checked hotels, hospitals, jails and morgues. After three days of unsuccessful searching, Mark's friends were asked to re-enact the events leading to his disappearance.
他以前的高中篮球队教练特里·雷说：“你总是知道他在外面做任何事，只要是马克，就一定会没事的。”马克的叔叔在洛杉矶的美国海关服务局工作，利用自己的人脉为他侄子的失踪吸引更多关注。尽管美国警方没有在墨西哥调查的管辖权，但在布朗斯维尔还是成立了一个负责搜救的工作组。墨西哥警方试图通过声称马克在德克萨斯州失踪来转移责任，尽管他的朋友们坚决否认这些说法。意识到这起事件可能会阻碍春假狂欢者重返马塔莫罗斯，政府官员向当地警方施压要求其采取行动。在马克失踪后的小时内，墨西哥联邦和州司法警察加入了美国工作组，作为双方边境的调查人员检查了酒店、医院、监狱和停尸房。经过三天徒劳的搜寻后，马克的朋友们被要求重新演绎导致他失踪的经过。

11
00:12:11.000 --> 00:13:11.000
As the last one to have seen Mark, Bill Huddleston was placed under hypnosis to see if his subconscious memory had retained any key details. He described walking past Garcia's and sighting a Hispanic male with a cut on his cheek and wearing a blue plaid shirt. The stranger motioned to Mark in English and he stopped to talk. Later, Bill told the Washington Post newspaper that he heard the man ask, Hey, don't I know you from somewhere? Bill clarified, it was just a glimpse. I don't even know if Mark answered him. Within days, texts and newspapers were reporting on the baffling case. The Kilroy family offered a $5,000 reward for information with James and Helen voicing concerns that their son may have been abducted.
作为最后一个见到马克的人，比尔·赫德尔斯顿接受了催眠，以查看他的潜意识记忆是否保留了任何关键细节。他描述说自己走过加西亚餐厅时，看到了一名脸上有伤口、身穿蓝色格子衬衫的西班牙裔男子。那个陌生人用英语向马克示意，马克停下来与他交谈。后来，比尔告诉《华盛顿邮报》报社，他听到那个人问：“嘿，我是不是在哪里见过你？”比尔澄清说：“那只是一瞥。我甚至不知道马克有没有回答他。”几天之内，文字和报纸都在报道这个令人困惑的案件。基尔罗伊一家悬赏 5,000 美元征集线索，詹姆斯和海伦对他们的儿子可能被绑架表示担忧。

12
00:13:11.000 --> 00:14:03.000
Helen explained, I'm extremely worried about him because he's pretty responsible. Being the person that he is, he would have contacted us or his friends. Mark was of legal drinking age and had joined his friends in consuming alcohol, but he had no interest in drugs. A devout Catholic, he took his faith seriously, often carrying a Bible that he'd read between studying. Although outgoing and fun, he was cautious and safe. Brent Martin, quote, I've known the guy ever since kindergarten. He wouldn't go off and just not call us. He's really smart. That's why this whole thing is so weird. Because as smart as he is, he would figure out a way to get in touch with us.
海伦解释道：“我非常担心他，因为他相当负责任。以他的为人，他会联系我们或他的朋友。”马克已达到法定饮酒年龄，并和朋友们一起饮酒，但他对毒品毫无兴趣。作为一名虔诚的天主教徒，他非常重视自己的信仰，经常随身携带一本在学习间隙阅读的圣经。虽然外向且有趣，但他谨慎且安全。布雷特·马丁说：“我从幼儿园就认识这家伙了。他绝不会就这样走开而不给我们打电话。他非常聪明。这就是为什么整件事这么诡异，因为以他的聪明才智，他会想办法和我们取得联系。”

13
00:14:03.000 --> 00:15:25.000
Police were starting to suspect Mark may have been attacked, robbed or fallen victim to drug-related violence and checked Matamoros' shanty towns and colonies known for their high crime rates. Bill Huddleston's hypnosis-induced memories led some to theorize Mark had been murdered as part of a botched kidnapping for ransom plot. As many tourists were still coming and going from the city, authorities were urged to solve the case quickly to ensure no one else felt victim to a similar fate. James Kilroy arrived in Brownsville, spending long hours each day speaking with investigators, developing strong connections with local reporters and handing out missing person flyers in South Padre and Matamoros, assisted by volunteers. Helen Kilroy remained by their home phone in nearby Santa Fe in case it rang with any news. Convinced that her son was being held against his will, she felt a haunting sense that he was being harmed every time she read her Bible. Quote, I've really felt strongly that somehow he's being hurt right now. I kept reading that nothing is impossible with God.
警方开始怀疑马克可能遭到袭击、抢劫或沦为贩毒暴力活动的受害者，并对马塔莫罗斯以高犯罪率闻名的贫民窟和社区进行了排查。比尔·赫德尔斯顿在催眠状态下唤醒的记忆让一些人推测，马克是被作为一场失败的勒索绑架案的一部分而被谋杀的。由于仍有许多游客进出该市，当局被敦促迅速破案，以确保没有其他人沦为类似命运的受害者。詹姆斯·基尔罗伊抵达布朗斯维尔，每天花很长时间与调查人员交谈，与当地记者建立牢固的联系，并在志愿者协助下在南帕德雷和马塔莫罗斯分发失踪人员传单。海伦·基尔罗伊则守在附近圣达菲的家中电话旁，以防有任何消息打进来。坚信儿子违背意愿被扣留的她，每次读圣经时都有一种挥之不去的阴森感，觉得儿子正在遭受伤害。她说：“我真的强烈地感觉到，此时此刻他正以某种方式受到伤害。我一直在读‘在神没有难成的事’。”

14
00:15:25.000 --> 00:16:49.000
I feel like Mark's going to come back to us. Whoever has him, I just don't want them to be so frightened that they would fatally hurt Mark. We don't have any anger toward that person. We just want Mark back. With everyone praying like this, I don't see how the Lord can refuse us. By Saturday, March 18, 80 officers were involved in the search. A police helicopter scanned the banks of the Rio Grande River as officers in four-wheel drives combed the brush-covered countryside on both sides of the border. 15 criminals known to operate in the area were questioned, including pickpockets and drug dealers. Possible links to other crimes committed over the spring break period were examined, including the murder of a Mexican truck driver, the abduction and sexual assault of a young American woman, and the violent robbery of another student, all of which occurred within five blocks of the Gateway International Bridge. In Brownsville, fundraisers increased the reward pool to $15,000, which was a significant amount in Matamoros, where daily wages averaged around $2 to $3.
“我觉得马克会回到我们身边。无论谁抓了他，我只希望他们不要害怕到致命地伤害马克。我们对那个人没有任何愤怒。我们只想要马克回来。大家都这样祈祷，我看不出主怎么能拒绝我们。”截至 3 月 18 日星期六，已有 80 名警察参与搜救。一架警用直升机在格兰德河沿岸巡视，四驱车上的警官们则在边境两侧灌木丛生的乡村中梳理。15 名已知在该地区活动的罪犯受到了讯问，包括扒手和毒贩。针对春假期间发生的其他犯罪行为的潜在联系也受到了审查，包括一名墨西哥卡车司机的谋杀、一名年轻美国女性的绑架和性侵犯，以及对另一名学生的暴力抢劫，所有这些都发生在网关国际大桥五个街区之内。在布朗斯维尔，筹款活动将悬赏金池增加到 15,000 美元，这在马塔莫罗斯是一笔巨款，那里的日薪平均在 2 到 3 美元左右。

