Helen Kilroy received a collect call from a man identifying himself as Danny, claiming to have seen Mark at a drug dealer's house in the city of Houston, Texas. Danny demanded $10,000 for all the information he knew. Helen agreed and arranged to meet him outside a gas station at 5pm the following day. Covert police officers overseeing the exchange noted several suspicious people milling around, but Danny did not approach. Another call came later that night, this time from a man calling himself Junior, who had noticed the police presence at the drop site. A second exchange was arranged for the next day at a nearby cemetery. Junior threatened to cut off Mark's fingers and send them to Helen if the police were notified this time. At 5pm on April 6, Helen went to the cemetery as arranged, once again under covert surveillance, but no one came forward to collect the ransom.
海伦·基尔罗伊接到一个自称丹尼的男人的对方付费电话，对方声称在德克萨斯州休斯顿市的一个毒贩家里看到了马克。丹尼索要 10,000 美元作为他所知道的所有信息的报酬。海伦同意了，并安排第二天下午 5 点在一家加油站外与他见面。监督这笔交易的便衣警察注意到周围有几个可疑的人闲逛，但丹尼并没有走近。那天晚些时候又打来了一个电话，这次是一个自称小尤宁的男人，他注意到了交易地点的警察。第二次交换安排在第二天附近的墓地进行。小尤宁威胁说，如果这次报警，他会切断马克的指头并寄给海伦。4 月 6 日下午 5 点，海伦按排好的去了墓地，再次处于秘密监视之下，但没有人出面收取赎金。

